     8	
     9	## The one rule and the evidence contract
    10	
    11	Every removed or replaced NFD character is checked at its original letter boundary. Canonical Unicode equivalence is unchanged. SF5 word-final elision aliases remain one atom, including next to real mark edits; other replacements count as deletions. Repeated signs keep their multiplicity. A spacing breathing attached as a combining mark still deletes the old spacing character, so SF6 can HOLD an otherwise valid SF5 atomic proposal.
    12	
    13	Combining/spacing marks require **reader AND detector**, or **reader AND recogniser text**. The coordinator’s **A∧B counts as one reader** in every mode, including PRESENCE/FULL; AE also retains its E check. Agreement is not independent print evidence. Apostrophes, quotes and numeral keraia require **detector AND recogniser text**; R1 supplies no punctuation absence signal. Other characters require a supported reader absence and a second source; no such reader head exists in the retained evidence, so these deletions HOLD.
    14	
    15	A reader absence needs a supported head, saved predictions from both A and B, scored coverage with a finite in-image span, a known evidence state, an empty uncertainty list, and no applicable slot/observation veto. Missing or conflicting B is not a reader absence, even if A and the detector agree. Detector absence needs an actually scored head, explicit `OBSERVED` coverage of the relevant region, a valid window, resolved localisation and segmentation, no unnamed or uncertain ink and no relevant clipping. Empty candidate lists without that evidence are UNKNOWN. The current apostrophe detector only scores word-final δ/τ/ρ/θ/π; an empty Ι, κ or μ slot is not a negative punctuation observation. Quote absence additionally needs the leading-left region observed. Keraia has no scored absence head in these saved records.
    16	
    17	Recogniser-text absence needs aligned letter context, a finite saved `recognition_confidence` in [0,1], a located in-image span, and no applicable uncertainty/clipping. An unscored string is not a positive absence. Its score is now included in the content-bound evidence envelope because SF6 consumes it. No missing confidence, coverage or observation state is filled in. This is evidence plumbing for the deletion rule, not a new source decision.
    18	
    19	Production changes: `release_gate.py` adds the deletion inventory/guard, policy id and score binding; `l1_common.overlay` records each decision and adds the whole-line HOLD before release. Existing composer functions and the SF5 text policy are byte/AST unchanged. All no-HOLD outputs retain their exact SF5 label and status. The verification checks this worktree and branch’s Git metadata separately from the shared common directory: concurrent other-worktree/branch changes and `info/refs` drift are recorded explicitly, not reported as globally unchanged. [Verification receipt](SF6_evidence/verification.json).
    20	
    21	## Held-out 666 — SF5 → SF6
