432:# One-command census addition once the pulled evidence lands:
433:$PY scripts/labelfix/sf6_measure.py --add-census /path/to/deletion_census.jsonl.gz
436:The census addition samples 30 distinct released-deletion lines with seed 6 from sorted IDs, writes source/hash custody, adds repository regression cases, replays both pools, runs all labelfix tests and refreshes this report and verification. It accepts JSON/JSONL runtime rows or L1R2’s aggregate `CHANGES.json`; the latter samples its AB deletion-example ID pool, not the full population. Aggregate IDs require a `deletion_witness_inputs.jsonl.gz` sidecar (record+runtime), or a full `overlay_ensemble_ab.jsonl.gz` with edit evidence and Google’s original labels available locally. Missing evidence writes a pending receipt and fails loudly; no source is reconstructed from guesses. The test harness validates both formats with independent 40-row fixtures. **census witnesses pending**. The read-only L1R2 report was checked at the end of this run: jobs prepared, no production job submitted and no pulled production census available; mock census counts are not substituted.
440:## SF6b — same-kind spacing-breathing MOVE
442:Before = **SF6**; after = **SF6b**. Policy id remains `sf6-release-v1`. Only `deletion_guard` changes in production: a consumed spacing psili (`᾿`/`᾽`) or dasia (`῾`) can MOVE to a newly written combining breathing of the same kind on the same capital, when A∧B names it with known, scored, uncertainty-free coverage inside the saved window and the capital has no existing slot veto. AE retains its E check. No positive absence is asserted for a MOVE. All other deletion checks, composer/slot decisions, observation gates, K1 and punctuation rules are unchanged.
444:Policy sha **`704c47a3ee5b742376b3c73a8dcf0722dc0077f48a839b1109355cf3980f360e`**, previously `544ad37c4b6c0c1e1c98a8c0d7642afc5c188bbd52e79aaf6eef0d1dce233460`. The existing `policy_binding()` hashes the changed source automatically; the replay passes this binding and sha to release overlays. [Policy and comparison receipt](SF6b_evidence/comparison.json).
446:The unchanged SF6 instruments were rerun twice from saved evidence: frozen launch sources for SF6, then SF6b. Every before line/check/metric reproduces the original SF6 evidence exactly. Original SF6 evidence and the pre-SF6b report prefix are preserved. No network, inference, `.git` writes or other-worktree writes. Launch HEAD: `b1104e3273e7d44acb95fe1d53495df0535f1a77`.
448:### Held-out 666 — SF6 → SF6b
465:No held-out label, status, check or slot outcome changes. Missing full runtime coverage remains unknown; it cannot qualify a MOVE. The 81,700 frozen slot/mode records remain identical. [SF6 replay](SF6b_evidence/before/heldout/metrics.json), [SF6b replay](SF6b_evidence/after/heldout/metrics.json).
467:### M2 DEV 273 — SF6 → SF6b
484:No M2 label, status, check or slot outcome changes. B/E remain missing; no replacement evidence is invented. Only the DEV allowlist is decoded: locked stratum (ii) decoded/composed **0**. Punctuation truth remains UNKNOWN. [SF6 replay](SF6b_evidence/before/m2_dev/metrics.json), [SF6b replay](SF6b_evidence/after/m2_dev/metrics.json).
488:| Cohort | Mode | SF6 → SF6b |
503:| Line ID | Cohort / mode | SF6 | SF6b label | Explanation |
517:The 56 SF5 witnesses now have 48 releases / 8 HOLDs (SF6: 46 / 10); the 48 L1A lines have 43 releases / 5 HOLDs (SF6: 41 / 7). All other witness outcomes and deletion checks are exact SF6 parity; the known reader mistakes remain HOLD. Quote probes remain **64/64 HOLD** and the keraia witness remains **HOLD**. No mark scoring is inferred for the witness cohort. [Full before](SF6b_evidence/before/witness_results.jsonl.gz), [full after](SF6b_evidence/after/witness_results.jsonl.gz), [per-line changes](SF6b_evidence/line_changes.jsonl), [changed checks](SF6b_evidence/check_changes.jsonl).
519:Released raw spacing-character removals change 0 → 2 per capital-witness cohort; all two are explicitly `operation=MOVE`, with the original absence signals still false. They are not content deletions. True released deletions remain 0 in held-out, M2 and these witness cohorts. Apostrophe/quote/keraia HOLD counts are unchanged in every cohort and mode.
521:The mismatched-kind control consumes spacing psili while proposing dasia, with no second certified psili-absence source: HOLD, no MOVE. The unnamed-reader control remains HOLD even for a forced attached-psili proposal. Unscored, uncertain, missing/conflicting B, clipped, unseen, outside-window, lowercase, already-attached, other-boundary and duplicate-sign controls retain exact HOLD assertions. Matching dasia is checked directly in the deletion guard; the unchanged composer/punctuation guard does not gain a new dasia rewrite route. [Concrete synthetic evidence](SF6b_evidence/synthetic_witnesses.json).
525:Full labelfix: **1260 passed, 1 environment setup error(s), 0 assertion failures**. The unchanged capture test cannot bind its loopback socket in this sandbox (`PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted`), also reproduced before the change (1100 passed, 1 error). All-green acceptance remains unmet in this sandbox; no test is skipped, deselected or weakened. [Before](SF6b_evidence/tests_before.log), [after](SF6b_evidence/tests_after.log).
527:Only the two released capital expectations change in existing regression tests; their output strings are exact. Existing unscored SF5 synthetic attachments still HOLD. The new positive MOVE tests fail on frozen SF6 (72 failures) and pass on SF6b (633 SF5/SF6 tests passed); all other SF6 absence tests are retained. [Frozen-SF6 failures](SF6b_evidence/witness_tests_before.log), [SF5/SF6 suite after](SF6b_evidence/witness_tests_after.log). Census witnesses remain pending; the original SF6 saved evidence is the measurement scope.
